<title>GERMANY: Hypo-Bank -provisions weigh on 96 profit.</title>
<headline>Hypo-Bank -provisions weigh on 96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Bayerische Hypotheken- und Wechsel-Bank AG said on Wednesday that its 1996 operating profit after provisions would drop around nine percent after risk provisions rose around 50 percent from year-ago levels.</p>
<p>In a statement, Hypo-Bank said that discounting provisions, net operating income had risen 17 percent in 1996, as net commission income advanced 43 percent to around 1.2 billion marks ($713.1 million) due to the consolidation of Foreign &amp; Colonial Management, its British fund management arm.</p>
<p>It also said it planned to keep its dividend unchanged at 1.45 marks per share. Full profit figures were not released.</p>
<p>($ = 1.682 German Marks)</p>
